   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# UTTA-Med: Phase 2.6 & Phase 2.7 — GPU Verification, Throughput Benchmark & 5-Seed Source Training\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook covers:\n",
    "- **Phase 2.6A**: GPU & CUDA Environment Verification\n",
    "- **Phase 2.6B**: GPU Throughput Benchmark with explicit `torch.cuda.synchronize()` and AMP across batch sizes (32, 64, 128)\n",
    "- **Phase 2.7**: Full 10-Epoch Source-Only ResNet-18 Training across all 5 frozen seeds (`[42, 123, 2024, 7, 99]`)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Frozen Master Plan Protocol Rules:\n",
    "1. **Source Training**: Centers `{0, 3, 4}` (302,436 patches)\n",
    "2. **Early Stopping**: Monitored strictly on OOD Validation Hospital (Center `{1}`)\n",
    "3. **Target Evaluation**: Center `{2}` labels touched **only after checkpoints are frozen**\n",
    "4. **Seed Matrix**: `SEEDS = [42, 123, 2024, 7, 99]`\n",
    "5. **Artifacts**: Every seed creates independent artifacts (`config.yaml`, `command.txt`, `git_commit.txt`, `metrics.json`, `checkpoint.pt`, `logs/`)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 2.6A — GPU Environment Verification"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Phase 2.6A: Verify exact CUDA and GPU device environment\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "print(\"PHASE 2.6A: GPU ENVIRONMENT VERIFICATION\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)\n",
    "print(f\"PyTorch version : {torch.__version__}\")\n",
    "print(f\"CUDA available  : {torch.cuda.is_available()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"CUDA version    : {torch.version.cuda}\")\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    print(f\"GPU             : {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Device count    : {torch.cuda.device_count()}\")\n",
    "    props = torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0)\n",
    "    print(f\"VRAM (Total)    : {props.total_memory / (1024**3):.2f} GB\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Compute Cap.    : {props.major}.{props.minor}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Multi-processor : {props.multi_processor_count}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    raise SystemError(\"CUDA GPU is required! Please change Colab runtime to T4 GPU via Runtime -> Change runtime type.\")\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 60)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Setup: Dependencies & Data Ingestion"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Mount Google Drive (optional) & install dependencies\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    from google.colab import drive\n",
    "    drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "    DRIVE_MOUNTED = True\n",
    "    print(\"Google Drive mounted.\")\n",
    "except Exception:\n",
    "    DRIVE_MOUNTED = False\n",
    "    print(\"Google Drive not mounted. Artifacts will be saved locally.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "!pip install -q pyarrow scikit-learn torchvision tqdm pyyaml huggingface_hub"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download official Camelyon17-WILDS parquet shards from Hugging Face\n",
    "import os\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from huggingface_hub import snapshot_download\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_DIR = Path(\"/content/Camelyon17-Data/data\")\n",
    "DATA_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "parquet_files = list(DATA_DIR.glob(\"*.parquet\"))\n",
    "if len(parquet_files) < 21:\n",
    "    print(\"Downloading official Camelyon17-WILDS parquet dataset (~10.7 GB)...\")\n",
    "    snapshot_download(\n",
    "        repo_id=\"wltjr1007/Camelyon17-WILDS\",\n",
    "        repo_type=\"dataset\",\n",
    "        local_dir=str(DATA_DIR),\n",
    "        allow_patterns=[\"*.parquet\", \"*.json\", \"*.md\"]\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "parquet_files = sorted(list(DATA_DIR.glob(\"*.parquet\")))\n",
    "print(f\"Verified {len(parquet_files)} parquet shards:\")\n",
    "for p in parquet_files[:4]:\n",
    "    print(f\"  {p.name} ({p.stat().st_size / 1e6:.1f} MB)\")\n",
    "print(f\"  ... (+{len(parquet_files) - 4} more shards)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 2.6B — GPU Throughput Benchmark\n",
    "\n",
    "Measures GPU training throughput with CUDA synchronization (`torch.cuda.synchronize()`) and AMP across batch sizes (32, 64, 128) to determine optimal batch size."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run Phase 2.6B Throughput Benchmark across batch sizes (32, 64, 128)\n",
    "for bs in [32, 64, 128]:\n",
    "    print(f\"\\n>>> BENCHMARKING BATCH SIZE = {bs} <<<\")\n",
    "    !python scripts/benchmark_training.py \\\n",
    "        --data-root /content/Camelyon17-Data/data \\\n",
    "        --batches 100 \\\n",
    "        --batch-size {bs} \\\n",
    "        --warmup 5 \\\n",
    "        --device cuda \\\n",
    "        --num-workers 2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Phase 2.7 — Full Source Training Across 5 Frozen Seeds\n",
    "\n",
    "Trains ResNet-18 across the 5 frozen seeds: `[42, 123, 2024, 7, 99]`.\n",
    "Each seed creates its own isolated experiment directory with all 6 artifacts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Frozen seed sequence\n",
    "SEEDS = [42, 123, 2024, 7, 99]\n",
    "\n",
    "for seed in SEEDS:\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
    "    print(f\"STARTING SOURCE MODEL TRAINING FOR SEED {seed}\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 70)\n",
    "    !python scripts/train_source.py \\\n",
    "        --config configs/source_resnet18.yaml \\\n",
    "        --seed {seed} \\\n",
    "        --epochs 10 \\\n",
    "        --batch-size 64\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nAll 5 source seeds successfully trained!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Artifact Packaging and Google Drive Sync"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Backup experiment metrics and checkpoints to Google Drive\n",
    "import shutil\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "if DRIVE_MOUNTED:\n",
    "    drive_dest = Path(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/UTTA-Med/experiments\")\n",
    "    drive_dest.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    for exp_dir in Path(\"experiments\").glob(\"camelyon17_resnet18_source_s*\"):\n",
    "        dest_dir = drive_dest / exp_dir.name\n",
    "        shutil.copytree(exp_dir, dest_dir, dirs_exist_ok=True)\n",
    "        print(f\"Copied {exp_dir.name} to {dest_dir}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Generate review zip containing code + configs + metrics\n",
    "!zip -r UTTA-Med-gateb-results.zip src scripts configs results experiments -x \"*.pyc\" \"*__pycache__*\" \"*.parquet\" \"*.pt\"\n",
    "print(\"Review zip created: UTTA-Med-gateb-results.zip\")"
   ]
